	% Incremental Potential Contact (IPC)~\cite{ipc} is a cutting-edge physical simulation method that has found widespread applications in mechanical engineering, robotics, and computer graphics. However, the performance of IPC remains a significant challenge, limiting the full potential of this robust and accurate method. To address the performance issues associated with IPC, several variants have been proposed, prioritizing improved efficiency at the expense of accuracy~\cite{2ndDec_ipc, pd_ipc, medial_ipc}. To accelerate IPC without compromising accuracy, \cite{gipc} proposed the first GPU IPC, GIPC. By harnessing the power of GPU, GIPC achieves significant acceleration while maintaining the required level of accuracy in IPC simulations.

