\paragraph{Methodology.}
The \emph{Inference Time} column captures the interval between the earliest and latest
timestamps in generation logs.  Cost was
computed as \(\text{Rate}\times\frac{\text{time (s)}}{3600}\).
Hugging Face bills by the minute, rounding up to the next minute\footnote{See HF
pricing page \cite{noauthor_pricing_nodate}.}.  All jobs used Hugging Face Text Generation Inference (TGI) as the backend.

\paragraph{Interpretation.}
Although the A100 delivers the fastest turnaround, its higher tariff narrows the
price gap: the L40S achieves the
best \emph{time–cost} trade‑off for our batch size, consistent with NVIDIA’s own
positioning of the L40S for high‑throughput GenAI inference \citep{noauthor_nvidia_nodate}.

