\subsection{Further work}
More details for the constructions of this paper may be provided in later
versions. Monoidal width, developed by Di Lavore and Sobocinski, may arise from
a slight generalization of the construction presented here
\cite{diLavoreSobocinski23:monoidalWidth}. It may be possible to connect this way
of timing processes to time-graded coalgebras of monads, which the authors have recently
proposed for continuous dynamical systems \cite{dilavore:graded}. 

