\section{A Framework for Seeing Feed-Based Social Media and their Protocols} \label{s_framework}
We introduce a framework to provide a consistent and accessible lexicon through which we can describe feed-based decentralized social media protocols. The framework's four \textit{architectural components} represent the technical infrastructure necessary for social media platforms to function; its six \textit{interaction components} are the socio-technical functionalities end users interface with.

