\subsection{Mathematical Calculations}
Consistent with the existing work \citep{frieder2023mathematical} that has demonstrated that GPT-4 can offer sufficient (but not perfect) performance for undergraduate-level mathematics, we note that specific mathematical calculations, such as the conversion between phasors and sinusoids, may be challenging for current state-of-the-art LLMs, including GPT-4o.

We provide the following example where intentional modifications were made to the correct solution of P 10.4-6 in \citep{svoboda2013introduction} to create a solution with arithmetic errors. We then tested GPT-4o to see if it could correctly identify the arithmetic errors in the solution independently, without the assistance of the official solution. 

