\textbf{Clarity in the title page and instruction section:} Both designers noted instances where the generated lessons inconsistently used terms like ``learners'', ``teachers'', ``tutors'', and ``students''. This inconsistency sometimes confused the intended novice tutors, as the lessons were specifically designed for training tutors on how to teach their students effectively. As shown in Table \ref{tab:lo_examples}, the examples generated by one-segment prompt fail to maintain clarity about the intended novice tutors—confusing ``learners'' with ``tutors''—and does not clearly address the objectives of the tutor training lesson. %This lack of focus detracts from the lesson’s clarity and risks misaligning the content with its pedagogical purpose. 
Such inconsistencies can hinder novice tutors' understanding of how the training content applies to their practice.


