\subsection{Timing and Convergence}
\label{sec:timing}
While this method is not yet real-time, we do report some preliminary timing results. 

Table \ref{tab:timing} gives the average wall time \textit{per gradient step}, per player, for each scenario. We average over 20 trials, otherwise using the same setup as in the previous experiments. (Note that the particle distribution updates take a negligible amount of time in comparison). Based on these results, we believe real-time execution is within reach, particularly as code optimization, GPU support, better handling of matrix sparsity, and improved parallelization all remain as potential improvements. 

