        \left(\frac{\langle 
    S_{t}, \theta \rangle - 1}{k^{1/2}(\|S_{t}\|_0 + 2)^{1/2}}
    \right)^{r-1} &\geq \left(\frac{\langle S_{t},
        \theta \rangle - 2}{k^{1/2}(\|S_t\|_0 + 1)^{1/2}}\right)^{r-1}. \\
    \intertext{Or, equivalently,}
        \frac{\langle 
    S_{t}, \theta \rangle - 1}{(\|S_{t}\|_0 + 2)^{1/2}}
     &\geq \frac{\langle S_{t},
        \theta \rangle - 2}{(\|S_t\|_0 + 1)^{1/2}},\\
        \intertext{which we can rewrite as,}
        1+\frac{1}{\langle 
    S_{t}, \theta \rangle - 1}
     &\geq\left( 1+\frac{1}{\|S_t\|_0}\right)^{1/2}.
        \end{align}And thus, a sufficient condition for the above displayed inequality to hold is,
        \[
     \|S_t\|_0 \geq \langle 
    S_{t}, \theta \rangle - 1
        \]
        which is trivial.

    Thus, the inductive argument is complete and the statement of the lemma holds for all $t \in [T^*_M]$.
