\end{corollary}

\begin{proof}
	By the exchangeability of $f$, we can restrict to the first $X$ output without loss of generality. 
	We then get\footnote{We write $X^\N$ instead of $X^{\N\setminus\{1\}}$ in the string diagrams to save space.}
