\section{System Architecture}
The system architecture comprises four layers (\Cref{fig:architecture}): the Data Injection layer, the Access Control layer, the Database Engine layer, and the Data Storage layer. 
%Each layer enables decentralized query processing, data storage, and retrieval.
Such a layered design provides modularization, and it also allows one to selectively decentralize any layer/component of their choice, thereby providing maximal flexibility such that different trade-offs between decentralization and performance (e.g., throughput and latency) can be sought in different use case scenarios. A modular design is essential to address such diversity in the Web 3.0 domain.

