\section{Results}

We find that transformer models, under certain hyperparameters and training distributions, are successfully able to learn the task of modular exponentiation to a high level of accuracy. The best performing model, seen in \autoref{fig:benford}, reaches an accuracy greater than 80\% after 3000 epochs.
