\subsection{Performance on the Exponentiation Task}
Uniform outcomes alone did not produce the best performance. Instead, sampling $a$ and $b$ log-uniformly sufficed for a good model, as shown in \autoref{tab:samplingresults}. We explain this with the class imbalance in the uniform operands setting, which can be resolved using log uniform operands without requiring uniform outcomes. In the following, samples are generated using reciprocal operands if not explicitly mentioned otherwise.

